3a.ee  CRITICAL 10.0  open-web
  A forged more-specific route to the web server of 3a.ee gets a certificate from any CA (1 of 1 addresses forgeable; 100% success in 5 attempts).
  fix first   domain-owner: publish CAA issue=<your CA>; accounturi=<your ACME account> → 1.1 Low
  to close    domain-owner + dns-host: publish CAA issue=<your CA>; accounturi=<your ACME account> + sign the zone and publish the DS at the registrar (DNSSEC) → 0.0 None

RISK CALCULATION   (design/formula.md)
  driving path   web → 3a.ee
  p              1.00   1 of 1 addresses forgeable
  P per attempt  1.000   = p × P(≥ 3 of 4 remote perspectives fooled)   [BR 3.2.2.9]
  likelihood L   1.000   = 1 − (1 − P)^5
  complexity K   1.000   = 0.87^0
  score          10.0   = Roundup(10 × 1 × K × L)   → Critical (CVSS scale)

